course: dictionary
lesson: 11532
title: Aloft: up high
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Aloft means up in the air, or held high above the ground. When you meet a word you do not know, read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «The balloon drifted aloft over the park, far above the trees.» The clues are drifted, far above the trees and the sky, so aloft must mean high up in the air.
explain: «The winner held the trophy aloft while the crowd cheered.» Here aloft means held up high. Check by swapping in your meaning: «held the trophy high» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Aloft can be an adverb or an adjective, so it can tell you where something is.
fact: «Aloft» means up in the air or high above the ground.
fact: «Aloft» can also mean held up high, as in «held aloft».
fact: On a ship, «aloft» means up in the masts and sails.
fact: Useful phrases: hold aloft, stay aloft, keep aloft and go aloft.
exercise: «The birds stayed aloft above the lake all morning.» What does aloft mean? | *Up high in the air | Swimming fast | Sitting on the water | Hidden under the trees
exercise: «The fans held their scarves aloft.» Find and copy the word that tells you the scarves were held up high. | fans | their | *aloft | scarves
exercise: The paper plane could ___ for a long time. Which phrase fits best? | *stay aloft | dig in | hold down | go under
test: «The sailor climbed up the mast to work aloft.» What does aloft mean here? | Down in the cabin | Under the water | Far out at sea | *Up in the masts and sails
test: Mia says aloft means low down. Is she right? | Yes, aloft means very quick | No, aloft means very wide | Yes, aloft means low down | *No, aloft means high up in the air
exam: Which sentence uses aloft correctly? | The flags lay aloft on the grass | The flags were aloft in the mud | *The flags flew aloft above the castle | The flags ran aloft across the road
